Build parking_lot_core with its `nightly` feature for the wasm build.

Reason: parking_lot_core 0.9.12 picks its wasm thread parker at compile
time. Without the `nightly` feature it uses thread_parker/wasm.rs, which
panics ("Parking not supported on this platform") the first time a
contended lock has to park. @pnpm/wasm 12.9.1 is built that way, so pnpm
traps ("wasm trap … unreachable") under load in slicc-kernel. With the
feature (and target_feature = "atomics", which wasm32-wasip1-threads
has), it uses wasm_atomic.rs: memory.atomic.wait32/notify, which
pnpm/wasm/build.mjs then routes through the pnpm_atomic imports.
The dependency only enables the feature; Cargo's feature unification
applies it to every crate that uses parking_lot_core.

Upstream: not filed (Lars decides).
removeWhen: upstream builds @pnpm/wasm with parking_lot_core/nightly, or
parking_lot_core stops panicking on wasm without it.

diff --git a/Cargo.lock b/Cargo.lock
index 5d2f469..8bcae11 100644
--- a/Cargo.lock
+++ b/Cargo.lock
@@ -4640,6 +4640,7 @@ dependencies = [
  "node-semver",
  "owo-colors",
  "p256",
+ "parking_lot_core",
  "pathdiff",
  "pep440_rs",
  "percent-encoding",
diff --git a/pnpm/crates/cli/Cargo.toml b/pnpm/crates/cli/Cargo.toml
index 4bd73ae..7d44820 100644
--- a/pnpm/crates/cli/Cargo.toml
+++ b/pnpm/crates/cli/Cargo.toml
@@ -168,6 +168,7 @@ reqwest = { workspace = true }
 tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["net", "process", "signal"] }
 
 [target.'cfg(target_family = "wasm")'.dependencies]
+parking_lot_core = { version = "0.9.12", features = ["nightly"] }
 pnpm-which = { workspace = true }
 pnpm-wasm-host = { path = "../wasm-host" }
 libc = { workspace = true }
